<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Azad Khan Afghan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1781">1781</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Azad Khan Afghan was an Afghan commander who rose to power in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a>. He was one of the main rivals of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karim-khan-zand">Karim Khan Zand</a> in the struggle for Iran. His defeat helped clear the way for the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zand-dynasty">Zand Empire</a>.</p></div>
